1	# @shortcut/mcp
2	
3	<img height="125" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7c3d3b8e-6252-4790-81cd-6640cd46a2d6" alt="Shortcut's logo" align="right">
4	
5	[![Version](https://badge.fury.io/js/@shortcut%2Fmcp.svg)](https://badge.fury.io/js/@shortcut%2Fmcp)
6	[![Monthly Downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/@shortcut%2Fmcp)](https://www.npmjs.org/package/@shortcut%2Fmcp)
7	[![GitHub License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)](https://github.com/useshortcut/mcp-server-shortcut/blob/main/LICENSE)
8	[![PRs welcome!](https://img.shields.io/badge/PRs-welcome-brightgreen.svg)]()
9	[![X](https://img.shields.io/twitter/follow/shortcut.svg?label=Follow%20@shortcut)](https://twitter.com/intent/follow?screen_name=shortcut)
10	
11	MCP Server for [Shortcut](https://shortcut.com) users.
12	
13	Links: [Local Installations](docs/local-server.md) | [ Server Developers](docs/developer.md)
14	
15	## Usage
16	
17	### Cursor
18	
19	The fastest way to get started is to connect to Shortcut's hosted MCP server. No API token or local setup required — authentication is handled via OAuth.
20	
21	1. Open (or create) the `mcp.json` file (it should be in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` or `<project-root>/.cursor/mcp.json`, but see [Cursor docs](https://docs.cursor.com/context/model-context-protocol) for more details).
22	2. Add the following details and save the file:
23	
24	```json
25	{
26	  "mcpServers": {
27	    "shortcut": {
28	      "url": "https://mcp.shortcut.com/mcp"
29	    }
30	  }
31	}
32	```
33	
34	3. Restart Cursor. You will be prompted to authorize with your Shortcut account on first use.
35	
36	### VS Code
37	
38	If all you need need the configuration for the mcp.json file use this. You will be prompted to authorize with your Shortcut account on first use.
39	
40	
41	```json
42	{
43	  "servers": {
44	    "github-mcp": {
45	      "type": "http",
46	      "url": "https://mcp.shortcut.com/mcp"
47	    }
48	  }
49	}
50	```
51	
52	For more detail on installing MCP services in VSCode see the [official VS Code MCP docs](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/copilot/chat/mcp-servers) for more information.
53	
54	### Claude Desktop
55	
56	Download the package [from this repo](https://github.com/useshortcut/mcp-server-shortcut/raw/refs/heads/main/mcp-server-shortcut.mcpb)
57	
58	Then, either double-click the icon to install or drag the package onto the client window. It should trigger the installation.
59	
60	### Other IDEs / Running Locally
61	
62	If your IDE doesn't support HTTP-based MCP servers, or you'd prefer to run the server locally, see the [Local Server Setup](docs/local-server.md) guide. This covers setup for **Windsurf**, **Zed**, **Claude Code**, and any IDE that supports stdio-based MCP servers.
63	
64	## Available Tools
65	
66	### Stories
67	
68	| Tool | Description |
69	|------|-------------|
70	| `stories-get-by-id` | Get a single Shortcut story by ID |
71	| `stories-get-history` | Get the change history for a story |
72	| `stories-search` | Find Shortcut stories with filtering and search options |
73	| `stories-get-branch-name` | Get the recommended branch name (based on workspace settings) for a specific story |
74	| `stories-create` | Create a new Shortcut story |
75	| `stories-update` | Update an existing Shortcut story |
76	| `stories-upload-file` | Upload a file and link it to a story |
77	| `stories-assign-current-user` | Assign the current user as the owner of a story |
78	| `stories-unassign-current-user` | Unassign the current user as the owner of a story |
79	| `stories-create-comment` | Create a comment on a story |
80	| `stories-create-subtask` | Add a new sub-task to a story |
81	| `stories-add-subtask` | Add an existing story as a sub-task |
82	| `stories-remove-subtask` | Remove a sub-task from a story |
83	| `stories-add-task` | Add a task to a story |
84	| `stories-update-task` | Update a task in a story |
85	| `stories-add-relation` | Add a story relationship (relates to, blocks, duplicates, etc.) |
86	| `stories-add-external-link` | Add an external link to a Shortcut story |
87	| `stories-remove-external-link` | Remove an external link from a Shortcut story |
88	| `stories-set-external-links` | Replace all external links on a story with a new set of links |
89	| `stories-get-by-external-link` | Find all stories that contain a specific external link |
90	
91	### Labels
92	
93	| Tool | Description |
94	|------|-------------|
95	| `labels-list` | List all labels in the Shortcut workspace |
96	| `labels-get-stories` | Get all stories with a specific label |
97	| `labels-create` | Create a new label in Shortcut |
98	
99	### Custom Fields
100	
101	| Tool | Description |
102	|------|-------------|
103	| `custom-fields-list` | List all custom fields in the workspace with their possible values |
104	
105	### Epics
106	
107	| Tool | Description |
108	|------|-------------|
109	| `epics-get-by-id` | Get a Shortcut epic by ID |
110	| `epics-search` | Find Shortcut epics with filtering and search options |
111	| `epics-create` | Create a new Shortcut epic |
112	| `epics-update` | Update an existing Shortcut epic |
113	| `epics-delete` | Delete a Shortcut epic |
114	  
115	### Iterations
116	
117	| Tool | Description |
118	|------|-------------|
119	| `iterations-get-stories` | Get stories in a specific iteration by iteration ID |
120	| `iterations-get-by-id` | Get a Shortcut iteration by ID |
121	| `iterations-search` | Find Shortcut iterations with filtering and search options |
122	| `iterations-create` | Create a new Shortcut iteration with start/end dates |
123	| `iterations-update` | Update an existing Shortcut iteration |
124	| `iterations-delete` | Delete a Shortcut iteration |
125	| `iterations-get-active` | Get active iterations for the current user based on team memberships |
126	| `iterations-get-upcoming` | Get upcoming iterations for the current user based on team memberships |
127	
128	### Objectives
129	
130	| Tool | Description |
131	|------|-------------|
132	| `objectives-get-by-id` | Get a Shortcut objective by ID |
133	| `objectives-search` | Find Shortcut objectives with filtering and search options |
134	
135	### Teams
136	
137	| Tool | Description |
138	|------|-------------|
139	| `teams-get-by-id` | Get a Shortcut team by ID |
140	| `teams-list` | List all Shortcut teams |
141	
142	### Projects
143	
144	| Tool | Description |
145	|------|-------------|
146	| `projects-list` | List all projects in the Shortcut workspace |
147	| `projects-get-by-id` | Get a Shortcut project by public ID |
148	| `projects-get-stories` | Get all stories in a specific project |
149	
150	### Workflows
151	
152	| Tool | Description |
153	|------|-------------|
154	| `workflows-get-default` | Get the default workflow for a specific team or the workspace default |
155	| `workflows-get-by-id` | Get a Shortcut workflow by ID |
156	| `workflows-list` | List all Shortcut workflows |
157	
158	### Users
159	
160	| Tool | Description |
161	|------|-------------|
162	| `users-get-current` | Get the current user information |
163	| `users-get-current-teams` | Get a list of teams where the current user is a member |
164	| `users-list` | Get all workspace users |
165	
166	### Documents
167	
168	| Tool | Description |
169	|------|-------------|
170	| `documents-create` | Create a new document in Shortcut with Markdown content |
171	| `documents-update` | Update content of an existing document by its ID |
172	| `documents-list` | List all documents in Shortcut |
173	| `documents-search` | Search for documents |
174	| `documents-get-by-id` | Retrieve a specific document in markdown format by its ID |
175	
176	## Limit tools
177	
178	You can limit the tools available to the LLM by setting the `SHORTCUT_TOOLS` environment variable to a comma-separated list.
179	
180	- Tools can be limited by entity type by just adding the entity, eg `stories` or `epics`.
181	- Individual tools can also be limitied by their full name, eg `stories-get-by-id` or `epics-search`.
182	
183	By default, all tools are enabled.
184	
185	Example (when running locally):
186	
187	```json
188	{
189	  "mcpServers": {
190	    "shortcut": {
191	      "command": "npx",
192	      "args": [
193	        "-y",
194	        "@shortcut/mcp@latest"
195	      ],
196	      "env": {
197	        "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN": "<YOUR_SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN>",
198	        "SHORTCUT_TOOLS": "stories,epics,iterations-create"
199	      }
200	    }
201	  }
202	}
203	```
204	
205	The following values are accepted in addition to the full tool names listed above under [Available Tools](#available-tools):
206	
207	- `users`
208	- `stories`
209	- `epics`
210	- `iterations`
211	- `labels`
212	- `custom-fields`
213	- `objectives`
214	- `teams`
215	- `projects`
216	- `workflows`
217	- `documents`
218	
219	## Read-only mode
220	
221	You can run the MCP server in read-only mode by setting the `SHORTCUT_READONLY` environment variable to `true`. This will disable all tools that modify data in Shortcut.
222	
223	Example (when running locally):
224	
225	```json
226	{
227	  "mcpServers": {
228	    "shortcut": {
229	      "command": "npx",
230	      "args": [
231	        "-y",
