172	### Documents
173	
174	| Tool | Description |
175	|------|-------------|
176	| `documents-create` | Create a new document in Shortcut with Markdown content |
177	| `documents-update` | Update content of an existing document by its ID |
178	| `documents-list` | List all documents in Shortcut |
179	| `documents-search` | Search for documents |
180	| `documents-get-by-id` | Retrieve a specific document in markdown format by its ID |
181	
182	## Limit tools
183	
184	You can limit the tools available to the LLM by setting the `SHORTCUT_TOOLS` environment variable to a comma-separated list.
185	
186	- Tools can be limited by entity type by just adding the entity, eg `stories` or `epics`.
187	- Individual tools can also be limitied by their full name, eg `stories-get-by-id` or `epics-search`.
188	
189	By default, all tools are enabled.
190	
191	Example (when running locally):
192	
193	```json
194	{
195	  "mcpServers": {
196	    "shortcut": {
197	      "command": "npx",
198	      "args": [
199	        "-y",
200	        "@shortcut/mcp@latest"
201	      ],
202	      "env": {
203	        "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN": "<YOUR_SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN>",
204	        "SHORTCUT_TOOLS": "stories,epics,iterations-create"
205	      }
206	    }
207	  }
208	}
209	```
210	
211	The following values are accepted in addition to the full tool names listed above under [Available Tools](#available-tools):
212	
213	- `users`
214	- `stories`
215	- `epics`
216	- `iterations`
217	- `labels`
218	- `custom-fields`
219	- `objectives`
220	- `teams`
221	- `projects`
222	- `workflows`
223	- `documents`
224	
225	## Read-only mode
226	
227	You can run the MCP server in read-only mode by setting the `SHORTCUT_READONLY` environment variable to `true`. This will disable all tools that modify data in Shortcut.
228	
229	Example (when running locally):
230	
231	```json
232	{
233	  "mcpServers": {
234	    "shortcut": {
235	      "command": "npx",
236	      "args": [
237	        "-y",
238	        "@shortcut/mcp@latest"
239	      ],
240	      "env": {
241	        "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN": "<YOUR_SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN>",
242	        "SHORTCUT_READONLY": "true"
243	      }
244	    }
245	  }
246	}
247	```
248	
